---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const example = `curl https://genaicommunity.ai/v1/systemone \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $COMMUNITY_API_TOKEN" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{
    "model": "mys/laya-typed-decisions-GGUF",
    "state": {"message": "I was charged twice for the same invoice."},
    "questions": {
      "billing": {
        "type": "noul",
        "instructions": "Is this a billing issue?"
      }
    }
  }'`;
---

<BaseLayout title="Model API" description="Member API for Laya, Hopper, and Xor typed decisions, with per-request GPU usage metering." sourcePath="src/pages/models.astro">
  <article class="max-w-[72ch]">
    <h1 class="text-display-lg leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.04em] font-bold mt-stack-md">Community model API</h1>
    <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-lg mt-stack-md">Use Laya, Hopper, or Xor typed decisions in your own tools. The API is open to every approved member and reports allocated GPU seconds after each call.</p>

    <section class="mt-stack-lg border border-outline-variant bg-surface-container-low p-gutter">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-semibold">Available models</h2>
      <p class="font-mono text-tertiary mt-stack-sm break-all">mys/laya-typed-decisions-GGUF</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">Laya specializes in decisions about invoices, security incidents, customer service, and agent traces. This checkpoint supports English only.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-md text-on-surface-variant">Published weights: <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="https://huggingface.co/mys/laya-typed-decisions-GGUF">Laya Typed Decisions on Hugging Face</a> includes F16, Q8_0, and UD_Q4_K_M GGUF files. This API serves the F16 file. Source: <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya-typed-decisions">original Laya checkpoint by Convai Innovations</a> · <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="https://github.com/monatis/ggmlc/tree/v0.9.2/examples/laya">ggmlc runtime</a>. Apache-2.0 licensed.</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-tertiary mt-stack-md break-all">mys/laya-multilingual-GGUF</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">The full multilingual F16 checkpoint for typed choices, scores, and yes/no decisions across languages. It runs as a separate protected T4 app and has its own usage total.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">The upstream model ships uncalibrated and is weak on zero-shot typed-decisions benchmarks. Validate its answers on your language and workflow before treating probabilities as thresholds.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-md text-on-surface-variant">Published weights: <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="https://huggingface.co/mys/laya-multilingual-GGUF">Laya Multilingual on Hugging Face</a> includes F16, Q8_0, and UD_Q4_K_M GGUF files. This API serves the full F16 file. Source: <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya-multilingual">original Laya checkpoint by Convai Innovations</a> · <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="https://github.com/monatis/ggmlc/tree/v0.9.2/examples/laya">ggmlc runtime</a>. Apache-2.0 licensed.</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-tertiary mt-stack-md break-all">HopitAI/hopper</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">Calibrated one-pass typed decisions on a separate protected A10 app. This uses Hopper's pinned BF16 fast-kernel runtime. Experimental BF16 and Q8_0 GGUF ports were built, but failed fidelity and p95 latency checks; they are neither published nor used for live inference.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">Hopper accepts exactly one typed question per call. For choices, provide a criteria map of option labels to descriptions; for scores, provide an array of level descriptions. Yes/no questions may omit criteria.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-md text-on-surface-variant">Source: <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="https://huggingface.co/HopitAI/hopper">Hopper adapter</a> · <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="https://github.com/hopit-ai/hopper/tree/v1.1.0">Hopper v1.1.0 runtime</a>. Apache-2.0 licensed.</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-tertiary mt-stack-md break-all">juspay/xor</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">Xor evaluates typed choices, ordinal scores, and yes/no questions over text and images. It uses the released BF16 checkpoint and calibrated SGLang wrapper on one protected NVIDIA A100 80GB, scaling to zero when idle.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-md text-on-surface-variant">Source: <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="https://huggingface.co/juspay/xor">Xor checkpoint by Juspay</a> · <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang">SGLang runtime</a>. Apache-2.0 licensed.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-md text-on-surface-variant">For inference and usage requests, use the four registry names shown in monospace above.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="border-y border-outline-variant mt-stack-lg py-stack-md grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-stack-md">
      <div><p class="font-mono text-label-caps uppercase text-on-surface-variant">Catalog</p><p class="font-mono text-tertiary mt-2">4 models</p></div>
      <div><p class="font-mono text-label-caps uppercase text-on-surface-variant">Runtime</p><p class="mt-2">ggmlc, Hopper, and SGLang</p></div>
      <div><p class="font-mono text-label-caps uppercase text-on-surface-variant">Meter</p><p class="mt-2">Allocated GPU seconds</p></div>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-stack-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-semibold">Get access</h2>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">Sign in with LinkedIn on <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="/apply">Apply</a>. Once approved, generate your application token there. Use the same token for model requests, sent as <code class="text-tertiary">Authorization: Bearer</code>. New tokens last 30 days. Existing tokens keep their original expiry. Regenerating your token revokes the previous one. Keep the token out of source code, logs, and URLs.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">If you use Python <code class="text-tertiary">urllib</code>, send a descriptive <code class="text-tertiary">User-Agent</code> such as <code class="text-tertiary">my-app/1.0</code>. Cloudflare rejects the library's default <code class="text-tertiary">Python-urllib/...</code> signature before the API can check your token. Python <code class="text-tertiary">requests</code> already sends an accepted User-Agent by default.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-stack-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-semibold">List models</h2>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant"><code class="text-tertiary">GET /v1/models</code> returns every available model with its exact name, source links, runtime, license, and GPU. Use your application token to call it.</p>
      <pre class="bg-surface-container-low border border-outline-variant p-gutter mt-stack-md overflow-x-auto text-code-sm"><code>curl https://genaicommunity.ai/v1/models \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $COMMUNITY_API_TOKEN"</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-stack-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-semibold">Make a decision</h2>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">Send the state you want evaluated and a map of typed questions. The required <code class="text-tertiary">model</code> field selects which model to call.</p>
      <pre class="bg-surface-container-low border border-outline-variant p-gutter mt-stack-md overflow-x-auto text-code-sm text-on-surface"><code>{example}</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-stack-md text-on-surface-variant">For multilingual input, use the same request with <code class="text-tertiary">"model": "mys/laya-multilingual-GGUF"</code> and put your text and question instructions in the desired language.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">For Hopper, set <code class="text-tertiary">"model": "HopitAI/hopper"</code> and send one question. Its answer uses the same top-level <code class="text-tertiary">answers</code> structure.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">For Xor, set <code class="text-tertiary">"model": "juspay/xor"</code>, supply <code class="text-tertiary">state</code> as text, and use an ordered array of 2–26 level descriptions for a <code class="text-tertiary">score</code> question. Optional <code class="text-tertiary">images</code> accepts up to eight static PNG, JPEG, or WebP base64 data URLs. Images are limited to 5 MiB decoded and 16 megapixels combined; the full JSON request is limited to 8 MiB.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">The response includes top-level <code class="text-tertiary">model</code>, <code class="text-tertiary">answers</code>, and <code class="text-tertiary">usage</code>, matching the SystemOne response convention. Usage includes <code class="text-tertiary">input_tokens</code> and <code class="text-tertiary">output_tokens</code> plus our GPU extensions: <code class="text-tertiary">gpuSeconds</code> for this call, <code class="text-tertiary">totalGpuSeconds</code> for your account, and <code class="text-tertiary">requestCount</code>.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">Usage includes the GPU type and count, its seconds unit, and <code class="text-tertiary">measurement: "inference"</code>. GPU seconds equal measured inference time times GPU count. A completed model call is metered even if the model rejects its input. A cold Xor app may return <code class="text-tertiary">503 model_starting</code>; retry after the <code class="text-tertiary">Retry-After</code> interval.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-stack-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-semibold">Read your usage</h2>
      <pre class="bg-surface-container-low border border-outline-variant p-gutter mt-stack-md overflow-x-auto text-code-sm"><code>curl "https://genaicommunity.ai/v1/models/usage?model=mys%2Flaya-typed-decisions-GGUF" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $COMMUNITY_API_TOKEN"</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">Replace the model query value with <code class="text-tertiary">mys%2Flaya-multilingual-GGUF</code>, <code class="text-tertiary">HopitAI%2Fhopper</code>, or <code class="text-tertiary">juspay%2Fxor</code> for separate totals. GPU seconds measure elapsed inference time inside the allocated GPU container. Startup, time waiting outside the container, and idle time are excluded. This meter does not measure GPU utilization or billed usage. Your totals belong to your member account, so they stay the same when you renew your token.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-stack-lg border-t border-outline-variant pt-stack-md">
      <h2 class="text-headline-md font-semibold">Endpoints</h2>
      <dl class="mt-stack-md divide-y divide-outline-variant border-y border-outline-variant">
        <div class="py-3 sm:grid sm:grid-cols-[260px_1fr] gap-gutter"><dt class="font-mono text-code-sm text-tertiary">GET /v1/models</dt><dd class="text-on-surface-variant">List models currently available to members.</dd></div>
        <div class="py-3 sm:grid sm:grid-cols-[260px_1fr] gap-gutter"><dt class="font-mono text-code-sm text-tertiary">POST /v1/systemone</dt><dd class="text-on-surface-variant">Run typed decisions and return token and GPU usage.</dd></div>
        <div class="py-3 sm:grid sm:grid-cols-[260px_1fr] gap-gutter"><dt class="font-mono text-code-sm text-tertiary">GET /v1/models/usage</dt><dd class="text-on-surface-variant">Get your total GPU usage for a model.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-stack-sm text-on-surface-variant">The older <code class="text-tertiary">/api/v1/models</code> routes remain available for existing integrations.</p>
      <p class="mt-stack-md"><a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="/openapi.json">Full OpenAPI specification</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
